Atari7800_MEGA65 - Atari 7800 (and 2600) for MEGA65
===================================================

MEGA65 port done in 2026 by Mikey351AU (with Claude)

https://github.com/Mikey351AU/Atari7800_MEGA65

Licenses: the MiSTer Atari7800 core sources in CORE/Atari7800_MiSTer keep their own license,
Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International (see CORE/Atari7800_MiSTer/LICENSE):
the core may not be used commercially. The MiSTer2MEGA65 framework and the port's own glue
(CORE/vhdl) are licensed under the terms of GNU/GPL v3 (see the file LICENSE). Other parts are
licensed under other Free-software licenses as described in the source code.

Atari7800_MEGA65:
-----------------

  Atari7800_MEGA65 is a port of MiSTer's Atari7800 core (release of 2 June 2026, commit 4372b3e3)
      done by the MiSTer Development Team
      Original GitHub Repository: https://github.com/MiSTer-devel/Atari7800_MiSTer
      Significant contributors:
      * Jamie Blanks (Kitrinx): k7800 (MARIA, RIOT, TIA, cartridge mappers, MiSTer core)
      * Mark Watson: POKEY (VHDL, 2013)
      * Jose Tejada (Jotego): JT51 (YM2151)
      * Daniel Wallner and others: T65 (6502 CPU)

Other than that and my own work, Atari7800_MEGA65 uses:
-------------------------------------------------------

  * MiSTer2MEGA65 by The MiSTer2MEGA65 Development Team
    https://github.com/sy2002/MiSTer2MEGA65

  * QNICE Co-Processor and System-on-a-Chip for file operations and on-screen-menu by The QNICE Development Team
    https://github.com/sy2002/QNICE-FPGA
    (M2M/rom/fat32_library.asm is a copy of its FAT32 library with a bug fix by this port)

  * bit2core from mega65-tools (LGPL v3) to write the MEGA65 core file header
    https://github.com/MEGA65/mega65-tools

  * Various MEGA65 drivers taken from the MEGA65 VHDL source by Paul Gardner-Stephen
    https://github.com/MEGA65/mega65-core

  * VGA Timing Generator, done by Scott Larson
    https://www.digikey.com/eewiki/pages/viewpage.action?pageId=15925278

  * VGA to HDMI converter IP core, done by Adam Barnes
    https://github.com/amb5l/tyto2

  * AVALON SCALER used for scaling to 720p for HDMI, done by temlib.org
    http://temlib.org/site/?page_id=10

  * HyperRAM controller, done by MJoergen
    https://mjoergen.github.io/HyperRAM/

  * Debouncer: I/O debouncing used for the joysticks, done by Scott Larson
    https://www.digikey.com/eewiki/pages/viewpage.action?pageId=4980758

  * Anikki-16x16 font, archived and provided by k80w
    https://github.com/k80w/consolefonts

  * PSF font to text file converter nafe-0.1 by Corvus Corax
    https://sourceforge.net/projects/nafe/

  * PSF font to C include file converter psftools-1.1.1 by John Elliott
    https://www.seasip.info/Unix/PSF/
